Booking started on a clinic's own site stays on that site (no new route).

Where: src/pages/[clinic]/index.astro (the `book` href) and src/pages/find/[clinic]/book.astro (header, back link, Done). Who: patients and clinic owners. Impact 3, effort S–M.

Problem: from /<slug>/, Book opens /find/<slug>/book/. That page has Flossify's patients' bar (Find a clinic, PhilHealth & HMO, My visits, Flossify's Clinic sign-in, Open your clinic), a back link into the directory (/find/<slug>/) and "Find another clinic" on Done. The patient changes place mid-task, and the clinic's own site hands its patient to a list of other clinics.

Change: the clinic site's Book links to /find/<slug>/book/?from=site, and the wizard carries the flag through its own links. With the flag, book.astro draws:
- `SiteHeader clinic={…}`, the same bar as /<slug>/: its initials and name, its sections, Staff sign-in to its door, the theme switch, and Book as the quiet twin;
- the back link to /<slug>/;
- on Done, "Back to <clinic>" (quiet) in place of "Find another clinic".

Without the flag, the page is exactly as today. /find/ links, a time held from /find/, /api/bookings and every saved link keep working. No RESERVED change is needed, because /<slug>/book/ would be a second segment anyway.

Must stay on both versions, word for word:
- the consent checkbox naming the clinic and Flossify, with the privacy notice link (RA 10173 transparency);
- the three-minute Undo;
- the Done line "cancel under My visits or by calling …" with its /me/ link. The clinic bar has no My visits, so this line becomes a patient's only way to cancel and must not be trimmed;
- the dev-only "Prototype" note that PatientHeader shows today.

Measure after:
- one teal button per screen, light and dark;
- contrast on the glass at 1440 and 390;
- no sideways scroll at 390;
- the bar's links resolve to /<slug>/#sections, not /find/.

Not an owner decision. It carries out his "every clinic gets its own generic site". The /find/ address was a default we announced to him, not his request. Tell him it was done, rather than asking first.

Draw today's visits once on each screen size, with short rows (Dashboard: index.astro #patients pane, patients.ts row(), board.ts list cards, cal.css).

**Phones (under 768 px):** show the day once. Today's patients is not drawn. The calendar's list cards take over:
- the row's one-tap step (Arrived, In the chair or Done, via stepOf and takeStep, keeping the consent ask through panels.askSeat);
- the allergy as a red pill in words;
- the alerts (conditions) as an amber pill in words, the first one plus "+N", not the icon-only cal-mark;
- the desk note icon, as now.

Both Calls and See all patients move to the foot of the list (or the calendar's head), so Calls keeps a way in on a phone.

**Desktop:** keep Today's patients as the queue beside the grid, at one or two lines per row:
- time · name · age;
- the status pill, with "Waiting N min" when the patient is on the bench (amber past WAIT_ALERT_MIN);
- the allergy pill and the first alert pill plus "+N";
- the step button.

The mobile number, "New", balance, "No next visit" and the full desk note move to the visit panel, which already shows them. A small note icon stays on the row when there is a desk note, as on the calendar card. The row's aria-label keeps every fact it has today.

**Check afterwards** with dash-check.mjs and the contrast tool:
- the phone's first card is above the 844 px fold;
- a row is 80 px or less at 1440;
- allergy and alert words are visible without hover at 390 and 1440, at 4.5:1 or better, light and dark;
- targets are at least 44 px;
- nothing scrolls sideways.

The desk loses the balance at a glance. It stays on the visit panel, the Collected today tile and Close the day.

Ask the owner before building. If the owner agrees: keep the printed poster at /f/<key>/ exactly as patients see it now, and run it on the intake machinery behind the scenes.

- **The poster's questions stay the poster's.** It keeps the full STEPS / FORMS_DEF set: about you, health, your teeth (the reason for the visit and the dental history), cards (PhilHealth PIN, HMO), consent. It does not use the shorter INTAKE_DEF page 1.
- **The poster's consent stays strict.** Both ticks are required, under 18 a named parent or guardian is required, there is no "Nobody here can agree" choice on the poster, and nothing is saved without the privacy consent. patient_form_submit (or its successor) still checks all of this again on the server.
- **The gates stay.** The formsNoticeReady / FORMS_PRIVACY_VERSIONS gate is unchanged. The owner is told that if the poster's general consent comes from the consent library, CONSENT_REVIEWED will also gate the poster on production.
- **One queue, "Forms to add", holds only:**
  - poster submissions;
  - desk intakes that already wait because they look like a patient on file (Screen F).
  It is counted in the inbox and on the Patients list, with Add / Add to <name> / Dismiss.
- **Desk-started intakes still make the profile at Send**, as the owner chose on 29 Sep.
- **Procedure forms** are offered only when the desk starts an intake, and only after the named dentist records "I explained this".
- **Carried over:**
  - nonce 'again' / 'resend';
  - the 500-per-poster 'full' cap;
  - the per-poster and per-address throttles;
  - autocomplete-off, with the contact tokens kept;
  - 30-day deletion of forms nobody adds, in retention_purge, matching the privacy notice's words;
  - retired keys saying 'replaced';
  - patient_consent rows of the versions in force, saying who signed, as whom and when;
  - the audit;
  - the 028 rows, channel 'form' and QR- references, readable and resolving on records and printouts.

Retire the old /patients/forms/ screens only once every old row shows in the new queue.

Finances (/c/<slug>/finances/): let the tiles be the filters.

Three tiles that are also the switches, built as the shell's Tabs in a tile style (role=tablist, aria-selected, arrow keys, the URL kept), so this is a variant of a pattern people already know, not a new one:
- Today: collected · charged. Opens today's statements.
- Still to pay: the amount in amber, "N patients · ₱X more from HMOs". Opens the unpaid list.
- HMO claims: waiting · overdue, with overdue in red and in words. Opens the claims section. Without finance.money it shows counts only, never amounts.

The chosen tile gets the teal tint, and its figure keeps its amber or red. This replaces the statements' Today · Still to pay · All · Void pill row and the Statements · HMO claims tabs.

Keep:
- one teal button per screen (New charge or New claim, following the chosen tile);
- the quiet Close the day button in the head (Collected today on the Dashboard already opens it);
- search and Download;
- the claims section's own Open · Drafts · Resolved · All and payor filters;
- the NOT_BIR line and the TIN callout;
- the audited CSV.

One plain line under the tiles, for the people who see the tiles today (finance.bill): "This month: ₱X collected · ₱Y charged · All statements · Void (n)". "All statements" opens ?view=all and "Void (n)" opens ?view=void. Void statements stay one tap away for the owner's check, not only through search or the CSV, because All shows at most 300 rows.

Every deep link (?view=today|unpaid|all|void, ?show=claims, ?claims=, ?payor=, ?patient=, ?q=) keeps working.

Measured on 4610 as the owner at session-road: 12 controls before the first row at 1440 (16 in all); at 390 the tiles take 296 px and the list starts at 556 px. Measure again after the change: controls, contrast on the tinted tile in light and dark, 44 px targets, no sideways scroll at 390.

Title: Split Clinic profile into "Your public page" and "How the day runs"

Where: /c/<slug>/settings/#profile. Files: settings/_ui/ProfileSection.astro, _lib/profile.ts (saveClinic), settings/index.astro (Which, SECTION_OF, the section index).

Problem: This is the section every owner lands on (Clinic settings, and /start/'s ?welcome=1). It is about 2764–2976 px tall at 1440 and 4849 px at 390, with 22 settings and 41 controls. It mixes three things:
- what patients see (listing, name, address, about, maps, HMOs, PhilHealth, walk-ins, founded);
- how the clinic operates (booking mode, chairs, the two text switches, and 044's gap between visits, held reminders and consent asked at chair or door);
- tax numbers.

An owner fixing a phone number scrolls past the reminder switches. One changing reminders reads the whole listing first. (The Save button is already at the top and the foot; the length is the problem.)

Proposal: two sections in the settings index, each its own form with Save at the top and the foot.
1. **Your public page:**
   - the listing switch and its "First add …" line;
   - the own-page and sign-in address box;
   - the Ready-to-be-found checklist;
   - name, city, address, phone, email, maps, about, founded, walk-ins, PhilHealth, HMOs;
   - Photos moved in below, still as its own separate upload, move and remove forms (no form inside another form).
2. **How the day runs:**
   - how patients book, dental chairs;
   - Texts to patients (the two switches);
   - Time between visits, Hold the reminder, Ask about a consent form;
   - TIN and BIR branch code under More. Not in "Your public page", whose title would suggest the TIN is published; it is printed on statements.

Server rules that must hold (the integrity part):
- Each half posts its own part (`form=public` / `form=work`). saveClinic updates only that half's columns. A field that is not on the form keeps its saved value, as `has_work_choices`, `form.has('tin')` and `form.has('founded')` already do. In particular:
  - a save from How the day runs never touches listed, clinic_hmo, walk_ins or philhealth_dental. A stray write there would unlist the clinic, delete its HMOs, or switch off the PhilHealth claims payor through the 013 trigger;
  - a save from Your public page never touches chairs, booking_mode, remind_48h, recall_texts or the 044 trio.
- `form=profile`, and the legacy post with no form field, keep saving everything as today, for tabs that are already open.
- The listing rule is unchanged (an about, hours and a dentist with days here; `held` note). It runs on every save, as now.
- holdClosedReminders still runs when the hold switch goes from off to on.
- Every save still writes the `clinic.settings` audit. The public half still writes `clinic.hmos_none`, because saidNoHmos is read from it.
- The TIN and BIR fields keep their sentence word for word: "Printed on statements from Finances. Flossify does not issue BIR receipts: keep using your own booklet or system." A refused tax save still opens More beside the field.
- Old anchors keep landing: #profile, #listing, #about, #hmos and #photos go to the public half; #work and #tax go to How the day runs. The welcome checklist's links still land, and ?welcome=1 opens the public half.
- The unsaved-changes guard names the right section.

Docs: update CLAUDE.md "How the day runs (044)" (Clinic settings → How the day runs) and HANDOFF.md rows 8 and "What to do next", which tell the owner the old place. Tell the owner where the three choices now live.

Checks: re-run choices-check.mjs and profile-check.mjs. Add a test that posts each half alone and shows nothing on the other half changed: listed, HMO rows, PhilHealth payor active, remind_48h, the 044 trio, TIN. Measure both sections at 1440 and 390 (estimated public half ~1250 px plus photos, operations ~1300 px).

Impact 4, effort M. Touches an owner decision: no, but the owner is told the new place.
